  "description": "Online sources for it-reelsmaker video edits: vertical stock footage (Pixabay, Pexels, Magnific), CC-licensed memes (Openverse; GIPHY as reference only), paid AI video generation (Veo, Kling, LTX via fal.ai) for B-roll, a cloud transcript (OpenAI), subtitle translation through the Claude, OpenAI or Gemini API, a narration in the person's own cloned voice (ElevenLabs), and figure cut-outs on your own server. Use only inside an it-reelsmaker edit, and only when the person names a cloud service, an API, paid generation, stock or online sources, or their own server, or turned these on: \"find stock footage\", \"generate an insert\", \"online memes\", \"transcribe it through OpenAI\", \"translate the subtitles through Gemini\", \"voice the script with my cloned voice\", \"cut out the figure on my server\". A plain \"transcribe\", \"translate the subtitles\" or \"cut out the person\" belongs to the core skill, which does it locally. Every download and paid run waits for the person's approval of the source, size and price.",
